![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When recomputing summary statistics from an array that may contain malformed or non-record entries, preserve the raw count of all elements for the total count, but filter the array to record-only entries before performing property-based filtering or aggregation. This prevents `TypeError` crashes when accessing properties on null or non-object elements.

```suggestion
export function summarizeMsSourceSelfAssessmentCaptures(captures = []) {
  const safeCaptures = Array.isArray(captures) ? captures : [];
  const recordCaptures = safeCaptures.filter(isRecord);
  const countWhere = (predicate) => recordCaptures.filter(predicate).length;
```

