![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

This refactoring addresses several critical correctness and robustness issues:
1. Destructures `receipt` from `options || {}` to prevent a `TypeError` if the function is called with an explicit `null`.
2. Explicitly validates that `sample_captures` and `source_artifacts` are arrays if present, recording an explicit invalid-type diagnostic to fail closed.
3. Explicitly verifies the presence and state of each expected element in `source_artifacts` rather than checking only the elements present in the array, ensuring validation fails closed if expected elements are omitted.

```javascript
export function validatePostAttemptMsSelfAssessmentRuntimeReceipt(options) {
  const { receipt } = options || {};
  const errors = [];
  const safeReceipt = isRecord(receipt) ? receipt : {};
  const counts = safeReceipt.done_criteria_counts || {};

  if (safeReceipt.sample_captures !== undefined && !Array.isArray(safeReceipt.sample_captures)) {
    errors.push('sample_captures_invalid_type');
  }
  if (safeReceipt.source_artifacts !== undefined && !Array.isArray(safeReceipt.source_artifacts)) {
    errors.push('source_artifacts_invalid_type');
  }

  const captures = asArray(safeReceipt.sample_captures);
  const captureErrors = captures.flatMap(validateMsSourceSelfAssessmentCapturePayload);

  errors.push(...captureErrors);

  const expectedRoles = [
    'frontend_integration_receipt',
    'frontend_integration_smoke',
    'frontend_integration_validator',
    'self_assessment_copilot_boundary',
    'self_assessment_copilot_boundary_validator',
  ];
  const artifacts = asArray(safeReceipt.source_artifacts).filter(isRecord);
  const hasAllExpectedRoles = expectedRoles.every((role) => {
    const artifact = artifacts.find((a) => a?.role === role);
    return (
      artifact != null &&
      artifact.exists === true &&
      artifact.loaded === true &&
      /^[a-f0-9]{64}$/u.test(artifact.sha256 ?? '')
    );
  });

  const dependencyPass =
    safeReceipt.dependency_status?.diagnostics_clean === true &&
    safeReceipt.dependency_status?.frontend_integration_receipt_issue === 1494 &&
    safeReceipt.dependency_status?.frontend_integration_validator_passes === true &&
    safeReceipt.dependency_status?.self_assessment_boundary_issue === 1461 &&
    safeReceipt.dependency_status?.self_assessment_boundary_validator_passes === true &&
    hasAllExpectedRoles;
  if (!dependencyPass) errors.push('dependency_artifacts_not_loaded_or_not_passing');
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When destructuring function parameters, destructure from `params || {}` rather than relying solely on parameter defaults like `function foo({ bar } = {})` if the function can be called with an explicit `null`. This prevents a destructuring `TypeError` and allows the `null` input to reach internal validation logic.
2. When validating lists of structured objects (such as artifacts), avoid relying solely on array length checks. Instead, explicitly validate that all expected roles or keys are present, and use defensive optional chaining to handle potentially null or malformed entries safely.
3. Ensure validators fail closed gracefully for null, malformed, or non-record inputs, validate manifest array fields and expected source artifact roles, and verify that upstream source files exist and parse as valid JSON.
</details>

